   "prompt": "Game interface concept art for a polished, shipped real-time tactics game, one flat portrait 2:3 image. World: an optimistic atompunk city in an alternate history, a 1950s world that discovered atomic power centuries ago, so its culture and style are 1950s but its technology is centuries ahead: clockwork, enamel and chrome instruments; never a touchscreen, hologram, glass blur or sci-fi neon. FINISH: professional AAA game HUD craftsmanship: crafted bevels, real enamel sheen with soft specular highlights, polished chrome trim with bright reflections, subtle depth, ambient occlusion and soft inner shadows, crisp edges, readable at 1080p; physical-object realism like a premium 3D-rendered control panel seen straight from the front. Palette: cream #f7f4ec and ivory #eee9da enamel, seafoam #72b5a7, deep teal #1f6c67, ink teal #17302f, polished chrome, a thin brass hairline only (never a large brass surface); turquoise #1cb9c6 only as a tiny indicator light. No red, no amber, no violet, no orange anywhere. Canvas rule: the whole canvas is one flat, perfectly even, solid magenta #ff00ff with no scene, no shadow, no gradient and no vignette; magenta never appears inside a piece. No text, no letters, no numerals, no logos anywhere on any piece. ROSTER STYLE: a TRAIN-CAB INSTRUMENT CLUSTER: a dark ink-teal satin panel with a chrome beaded edge, tiny chrome screws, and a seafoam enamel stripe. Draw exactly ONE piece, centred on the canvas, fully opaque, with at least 60 px of magenta all round: the ROSTER COLUMN, a tall narrow compact panel about 330 px wide and 1180 px tall (about 1:3.6), holding FOUR equal SQUARE portrait windows stacked top to bottom, each about 250 px square and filling about 76% of the panel's width, so the frame around them is SLIM; every window is filled with one flat bright lime green #00ff00 (the portrait goes there; lime appears nowhere else), each a perfectly round window like a gauge with a thick polished chrome bezel ring and a thin 